      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Untested Mock Controls / YAGNI**:\n\n`common/mock/hwtimer_mock.c` and `include/mock/hwtimer_mock.h` expose `struct mock_ctrl_hwtimer` (`clock_val`, `event_deadline`, `auto_increment`), `MOCK_CTRL_DEFAULT_HWTIMER`, the `if (mock_ctrl_hwtimer.auto_increment)` branch in `__hw_clock_source_read()`, and the event deadline hooks (`__hw_clock_event_set()`, `__hw_clock_event_get()`, `__hw_clock_event_clear()`). However, `test/timer.cc` never includes `\"mock/hwtimer_mock.h\"`:\n\n- `mock_ctrl_hwtimer` is never reset to `MOCK_CTRL_DEFAULT_HWTIMER` in `before_test()` in `test/timer.cc`, so mock state leaks across test cases.\n- `mock_ctrl_hwtimer.auto_increment` is always `true`, leaving the `false` branch in `__hw_clock_source_read()` (line 32) completely untested.\n- `__hw_clock_event_set()`, `__hw_clock_event_get()`, and `__hw_clock_event_clear()` (as well as the `timer_print_info()`, `command_force_time()`, and `command_get_time()` paths modified in `common/timer.c`) are not exercised by `test/timer.cc`.\n\nPlease either:\n\n1. **Add unit tests in `test/timer.cc`** that reset `mock_ctrl_hwtimer` in `before_test()` and cover `auto_increment \u003d false`, hardware clock event deadline set/get/clear, and the modified `common/timer.c` functions:\n   ```cpp\n   #include \"mock/hwtimer_mock.h\"\n\n   void before_test(void)\n   {\n   \tmock_ctrl_hwtimer \u003d MOCK_CTRL_DEFAULT_HWTIMER;\n   \t__hw_clock_source_init(0);\n   }\n\n   test_static int test_hwtimer_mock_controls(void)\n   {\n   \tmock_ctrl_hwtimer.auto_increment \u003d false;\n   \t__hw_clock_source_set(100);\n   \tTEST_EQ(__hw_clock_source_read(), 100U, \"%u\");\n   \tTEST_EQ(__hw_clock_source_read(), 100U, \"%u\");\n\n   \tmock_ctrl_hwtimer.auto_increment \u003d true;\n   \tTEST_EQ(__hw_clock_source_read(), 101U, \"%u\");\n\n   \t__hw_clock_event_set(500);\n   \tTEST_EQ(__hw_clock_event_get(), 500U, \"%u\");\n   \t__hw_clock_event_clear();\n   \tTEST_EQ(__hw_clock_event_get(),